    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T10:32:36Z",
    "body": "Additions from the independent read of PR #3684 (head `ac03087a3`):\n\n- The \"After the #3453 PR\" table in the body describes an approach that the PR dropped. The correction comment has the right numbers: window 0 is 2.7 mm below the floor, windows 1 to 3 are 18.0 mm with a 2.501 mm crescent.\n- The stay-down ramp preset is in scope here. Window 0 dives 13.5 mm with a 2.501 mm crescent. Then its lead-in arc feeds sideways at Z-18 through material that is cut only to Z-4.5.\n- A ring that shares a level with another ring or another band keeps its old seam (the exception of the PR). On such a ring window 0 enters as before the PR.\n",
